No!

257
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:08,680
We're too late.

258
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:10,526
They're all on their own now.

259
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:31,020
We're here! We're here!

260
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:33,537
The digital world is here! We're here!

261
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,897
We have arrived, children!

262
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:36,160
We are finally here!

263
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,110
It's real!

264
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:43,888
I've spent so much time
dreaming about this,

265
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:46,557
that finally being here
makes it seem as if I've

266
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,477
only fallen asleep and
returned to that dream,

267
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:49,390
but it's real!

268
00:11:49,473 --> 00:11:50,419
The dream is real!

269
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,757
The moment I've been
waiting for is finally here!

270
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:53,800
Ah, ah!

271
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:55,170
Huh?

272
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,417
What's the matter with you?

273
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,237
Why don't you play with
the other children?

274
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,150
This is wrong.

275
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,458
This is just wrong.

276
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:05,637
We're not really in the digital world.

277
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,896
What are you saying?

278
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,897
Of course it's the digital world.

279
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:10,560
No, it's, it's wrong.

280
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:14,960
Ah, wha, what is this place?

281
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:19,347
If this isn't the digital world,
then where have I brought us?

282
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,680
Acid mist.

283
00:12:23,220 --> 00:12:24,180
The... Razor!

284
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:27,240
I need time!

285
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:31,907
That was just a sample
of your parting gifts.

286
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,917
Yeah, now let those children go.

287
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:34,941
What's going on?

288
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:36,238
I don't understand.

289
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:37,370
It's gone.

290
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:39,226
What's happened to my dreams?

291
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:43,400
Hey, where are we?

292
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,460
I don't know.

293
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:47,057
Because Black War Greymon
shut the digital gate,

294
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:49,197
we must have ricocheted to another world.

295
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:51,357
But which world this
might be, I have no clue.

296
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,911
I've never seen anything like this before.

297
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,180
It's not fair!

298
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,478
I wanted to go to the digital world!

299
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:02,580
You can't always get
what you want, can you?

300
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:06,220
That's what I call a big mouth!

301
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:08,940
You can forget the digital world, Oikawa.

302
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,817
It is beyond your reach now.

303
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:13,782
You will never see it
again, even in your dreams.

304
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:18,000
Yes, cry. You are doomed.

305
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,617
For you have entered a world of despair

306
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:23,440
Where your souls will
be consumed by darkness,

307
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:27,545
and there is no place for you to
hide nor hope for you to escape

308
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:31,280
Who or what are you?

309
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:34,297
Are you working with Daemon
or some other weirdo?

310
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,360
Daemon? Ha!

311
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:38,857
Am I going crazy or is my
voice coming out of that mouth?

312
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:40,277
A bit of both, I think.

313
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:41,520
You see, I'm you.

314
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,837
What are you saying?

315
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,420
Three years ago, I was in need of a host,

316
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:48,600
and when I found you, I
used you to store my data.

317
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:51,140
Then you and I became as one.

318
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,520
Three years ago?

319
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:55,800
That was just about the
time my friend Hiroki died.

320
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:01,717
Yes, Hiroki, the friend over
whom you pretended to grieve.

321
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,777
But you secretly hated him, didn't you?

322
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:07,617
Hated him because the two of you had
promised to go to the digital world together,

323
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:10,197
but he left you all
alone. That's not true.

324
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,162
I could never have hated Hiroki.

325
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,480
Do you not remember?

326
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:24,040
Look, Hiroki, can you see it?

327
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:27,877
It's the digital world we were
supposed to visit together.

328
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,020
It's so beautiful.

329
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,082
Can you see it?

330
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:33,177
Why did you have to do it, Hiroki?

331
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:35,777
Why did you have to
die and leave me alone?

332
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,660
How could you do this to me?

333
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:41,380
The Digidestined.

334
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:42,800
Take me, too.

335
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:45,000
I want to leave this world.

336
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:50,660
Do you really want to
go to the digital world?

337
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:52,870
What's that?

338
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:54,650
Who's there?

339
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:57,377
If you really want to
go to the digital world,

340
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:00,597
soothe your heart with darkness,
and I'll take you there.

341
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,957
Yes, I'll do anything.

342
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,057
Anything you want.

343
00:15:03,140 --> 00:15:05,520
Just take me there, please. So be it.

344
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:11,660
That was you?

345
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:13,537
This whole time?

346
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:20,157
you've been inside of me controlling
everything I did I do so love iron me

347
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:26,620
my little marionette that voice what I
still hear that voice in my nightmares

348
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:38,077
but how can that be yes I'm
not surprised that you saw

349
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:41,297
through me my old pet but But
here's something you didn't know.

350
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:44,357
The Dark Spirals were based
on your own beloved tail ring,

351
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:47,558
so in a way, you caused
those Digimon to be enslaved.

352
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,697
I should have known that only your twisted

353
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:52,600
mind could come up with
a plan as evil as this.

354
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:55,368
If it takes my nine
lives, I'll destroy you.

355
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,912
Delightful, but you're so very misguided.

356
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:12,097
what's the matter are you
seeing double oh sorry got oman

357
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:15,517
got your tongue oh and by
the way about the dark spores

358
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,237
opening a doorway between the
worlds they're really just

359
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:21,217
the batteries that that will
allow me to finally be reborn.

360
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,130
Ew!

361
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:28,717
Please don't worry, I
won't destroy you yet.

362
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:31,977
I first need to harvest the dark
flowers growing inside of you.

363
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:33,531
I wouldn't count on that!

364
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:35,477
What are you waiting for?

365
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,390
Fight!

366
00:16:36,473 --> 00:16:37,303
Right!

367
00:16:37,386 --> 00:16:38,216
Oh, yeah!

368
00:16:38,299 --> 00:16:39,129
Spider-trip!

369
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:45,677
This dark flower had rose beef,
this dark flower had none,

370
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,557
and this dark flower
cried whee-wee-wee-wee!

371
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,217
That's really getting on my nerves.

372
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:51,124
Now, now, let him eat in peace.

373
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:52,720
And last, but not least,

374
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:55,620
allow me to reveal myself.

375
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,077
Look, he's...

376
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,060
He's changing.

377
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:05,140
But into Myotismon or Venom Myotismon?

378
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:10,900
Actually, you can call me Malomyotismon.

379
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,440
It's nothing but a deadly,
blood-sucking fiend.

380
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,280
Nothing is as evil as Malomyotismon.

381
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,118
What are you doing?

382
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,933
I've been your faithful servant, Master.

383
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:24,457
What do you think I'm doing?

384
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:25,880
Tell me. I don't know.

385
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,320
I think you do.

386
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:31,800
Show me what you're thinking.

387
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:36,560
Arokeny Mom!

388
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:40,040
What have you done to her?

389
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,697
I just did what she was thinking.

390
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:44,640
Now really, is that so wrong? Is it?

391
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:45,670
Please stop!

392
00:17:45,753 --> 00:17:49,177
Just because I was thinking it doesn't
mean I really want it to happen.

393
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:50,340
I love this game.

394
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,997
So tell me, what do you
think I'm going to do next?

395
00:17:53,080 --> 00:17:53,917
Think hard now.

396
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:54,830
I don't know.

397
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:56,717
I don't want to think about it.

398
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,260
But you already have.

399
00:17:58,400 --> 00:17:59,820
And it's a tasty idea.

400
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:04,880
Oh, get him on.

401
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:07,430
Don't hurt.

402
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,760
What next?

403
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,100
What should I do?

404
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,900
Show me what you fear.

405
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:15,320
Please, no. No! Not that!

406
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,620
Very well.

407
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:25,940
Are you killing one?

408
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,602
I'm afraid she's gone to pieces.

409
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:32,317
All I did was grant her her wish to
get as far away from me as possible.

410
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:34,518
Well, she'll never be near me again.

411
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:35,980
You destroyed her.

412
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,160
How could you?

413
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:39,260
Snack! Bandage!

414
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,137
You can't hide your fears, either.

415
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,297
You think you don't stand
a chance against me.

416
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:46,210
And you know what?

417
00:18:46,293 --> 00:18:47,457
You're right, you don't.

418
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:48,760
You don't scare me.

419
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,637
You've taken away my Arukenemon.

420
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:53,477
And now I'm going to make you
pay for what you did to her!

421
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:54,390
Ha!

422
00:18:54,473 --> 00:18:55,303
What you plan to do?

423
00:18:55,386 --> 00:18:57,497
Wrap me in another useless snake bandage?

424
00:18:57,580 --> 00:19:01,237
You scare me even less than these
Digidestined fools from the other world!

425
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:03,202
And I will teach you to fear me!

426
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:06,740
Playtime is over!

427
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:08,520
Crimson Mist!

428
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:19,460
Kari, time to digivolve.
You can't. Why not?

429
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:21,541
I don't want you to be destroyed.

430
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,780
Come on, guys, it's up to us to stop him.

431
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:27,920
I've never felt like this.

432
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,591
I've never been so afraid to fight before.

433
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,033
Can someone else fight?

434
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,580
Anyone else, please?

435
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,597
This is just a nightmare.

436
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:36,780
Soon I'll wake up.

437
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:38,437
What's wrong with you guys?

438
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:41,277
If we think we can't win, then all
of us are doomed from the start.

439
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:45,080
We'll win, but we've got to
believe in ourselves. He's right.

440
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,070
Don't worry.

441
00:19:48,153 --> 00:19:50,660
I'll fight him all by myself, Davis. What?

442
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:52,317
But you can't fight alone.

443
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,437
Hey, wait a sec.

444
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:55,177
You think I'm going to lose, don't you?

445
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:56,720
Well, maybe a little.

446
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:57,980
Believe in me.

447
00:19:58,180 --> 00:20:00,827
You've got to believe
that we can defeat him.

448
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:07,240
Right, let's fight.

449
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:11,557
Just imagine it's the last minute of a
soccer game and it's you against the goalie.

450
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:12,577
You know what to do, right?

451
00:20:12,660 --> 00:20:13,490
Not a clue!

452
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:16,380
Beat the bad guy! Right!

453
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:18,860
You don't look so tough!

454
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,630
Please!

455
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:25,750
Wait.

456
00:20:25,833 --> 00:20:28,460
Melomyotismon is too
powerful for XVmon alone.

457
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:32,980
We need to DNA digivolve,
right? Your hand. It's shaking.

458
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:35,197
I can't help it. I'm afraid.

459
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:39,398
Hey, we'll never be able to DNA
digivolve if you're afraid of it, Ken.

460
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:41,600
Now, I've got a bad guy to beat.

461
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,580
I, uh...

462
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:46,401
Now, don't say another word, Ken.

463
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:49,057
I know that you're afraid,
but you can't give in to it.

464
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,964
You can't let fear control you.

465
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:57,917
We've got to hide our fears from
Melomyotismon, or he'll use them against us.

466
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
We've got to.

467
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,860
Let's get him, XP-mon!

468
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:02,080
You will win!

469
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,540
You must defeat him!

470
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:15,020
I don't know.

471
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:36,460
I'll be wrong.

472
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,809
If you're with your hands,

473
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:44,360
you'll be running together.

474
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:48,280
Why do you want a big power?

475
00:21:56,280 --> 00:22:02,620
Every time, every time, I'll
be able to get you together.

476
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,370
I'll see you

477
00:22:22,453 --> 00:22:28,820
next

478
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:33,310
time.

479
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:04,200
We'll be back.
